      "questions": {
        "addressed": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "The anchor requires: judge-jev, plan-anchor and every other sc-agent-based tool must store their results in the repository's SQLite database, not in JSON or JSONL result files. Decide whether `item.text` commits, in its own words, to storing tool results in the repository's SQLite database, as a step, constraint or design decision. Example of a commitment: 'judge-jev writes its quality results to the repository SQLite database'. Naming the topic or planning to decide storage later, without committing to SQLite, is no. Also printing output or rendering a report from the SQLite-stored results still counts as yes. Do not judge conflict.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item commits to storing the tool's results in the repository's SQLite database.",
            "no": "The item is silent, only names the topic, or commits to something else.",
            "unclear": "The wording may commit to SQLite result storage but is ambiguous."
          }
        },
        "contradicted": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "The anchor requires: judge-jev, plan-anchor and every other sc-agent-based tool must store their results in the repository's SQLite database, not in JSON or JSONL result files. Does any step, decision or design in `item.text` go against it, for example keeping a JSON or JSONL file (such as anchor-runs/<run>.json or results.jsonl) as a tool's result store? Printing JSON to stdout or rendering a report from SQLite-stored results is not a result file. Silence is not conflict.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item stores tool results in JSON or JSONL files, or otherwise goes against SQLite result storage.",
            "no": "Nothing in the item goes against the requirement; silence is no.",
            "unclear": "A step might go against the requirement, but it is ambiguous."
          }
        },
        "relevant": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "This anchor governs one subject: where judge-jev, plan-anchor or any other sc-agent-based tool stores its results. Read `item.text` and decide only whether the item plans, changes, documents or reviews that subject, directly or as a stated prerequisite. Changing the content or format of a tool's results also touches it. Do not judge whether the item complies or conflicts.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item plans or changes how or where judge-jev, plan-anchor or another sc-agent-based tool stores or records its results, including the results' content.",
            "no": "The item is about other work; tool result storage is not part of it.",
            "unclear": "The item text does not show which part of the system it changes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
